        "subject": "LU-20476 o2iblnd: don't destroy a cm_id we still own",
        "message": "LU-20476 o2iblnd: don't destroy a cm_id we still own\n\nThe DISCONNECTED handler clears cmid->context but leaves the cm_id\nowned by o2iblnd, to be destroyed later by connd in\nkiblnd_destroy_conn(). The UNREACHABLE handler reads a NULL context\nas \"no conn has been created yet\" and returns -ENETDOWN.\n\nThat reading is wrong. The DISCONNECTED handler is the only place\nthat ever assigns NULL to a cm_id context. Before a conn exists the\ncontext is the kib_peer_ni passed to rdma_create_id(), so a NULL\ncontext at UNREACHABLE can only mean the conn has already\ndisconnected and is waiting for connd, which is exactly when the\ncm_id is still ours.\n\nA non-zero return from the handler tells the CM to destroy the\ncm_id. cma_netevent_work_handler() does so on any non-zero return,\nso a RoCE neighbour invalidation against a disconnected conn\ndestroys a cm_id that connd then destroys a second time:\n\n  general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address\n                                            0xdead000000000200\n  RIP: 0010:_destroy_id+0x18c/0x300 [rdma_cm]\n  Call Trace:\n   kiblnd_destroy_conn+0x29f/0x670 [ko2iblnd]\n   kiblnd_connd+0xfa/0x980 [ko2iblnd]\n\nReturn 0 instead. The conn still holds ibc_cmid and connd destroys\nthe cm_id before freeing the conn, so nothing is leaked.\n\nDestroy the cm_id before dropping the peer_ni reference in\nkiblnd_destroy_conn(). A CM callback may still be running on the\ncm_id and may dereference conn->ibc_peer. rdma_destroy_id() waits\nfor in-flight handlers to complete.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4.8\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 47b4886e12 (\"LU-18897 o2iblnd: NULL pointer dereference\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I11f0911b1aaa6c2816a1257ad2162a9d35257473\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
